<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- increased-memory-limit entitlement removed 2026-08-14 for the DAT capture test build:
         it blocked the auto-provisioning profile, and the on-device Gemma VLM path is unused
         (backend = brain.intch.cc). Restore if local MLX models are needed. -->

    <!-- AUR-845b: the SSID name in `phone.status`. Held back on 2026-08-21 morning because the app
         was signing against the XC wildcard profile ("iOS Team Provisioning Profile: *"), which
         carries no capabilities at all — adding this key failed the device build outright. The
         explicit App ID `app.soulless.openvision` (4DUB6L4475, team 3JAHQ7PYLM) now exists WITH
         Access Wi-Fi Information enabled, so the key can land: automatic signing has to pick the
         explicit App ID to satisfy it, which is exactly what we want.
         Key verified against Xcode's own capability bundle (ACCESS_WIFI_INFORMATION →
         com.apple.developer.networking.wifi-info, BOOLEAN true), not from memory.
         Without it NEHotspotNetwork.fetchCurrent() returns nil and PhoneStatusTool reports
         ssidMiss: "entitlement" — the honest miss it was written to report. -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.networking.wifi-info</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- ShazamKit has NO entitlement key to add here, and this is a measured fact, not an omission.
         SHAZAM_KIT is enabled on the App ID (App Store Connect API, 2026-08-21:
         bundleId 4DUB6L4475 → capabilities IN_APP_PURCHASE, SHAZAM_KIT, ACCESS_WIFI_INFORMATION),
         but it is an App SERVICE, not a profile capability: the development profile Apple issued
         MINUTES after the toggle ("iOS Team Provisioning Profile: app.soulless.openvision",
         3481d879…) carries wifi-info and does NOT carry com.apple.developer.shazamkit. Adding the
         key anyway fails the device build outright:
           error: Entitlement com.apple.developer.shazamkit not found and could not be included in
           profile. This likely is not a valid entitlement and should be removed from your
           entitlements file.
         Xcode 26.5 agrees — its own capability bundle (UserData/Capabilities) has 192 capabilities
         and no SHAZAM_KIT among them, and the string "com.apple.developer.shazamkit" appears
         nowhere in Xcode. ShazamKit is authorised server-side by bundle id via the App Service.
         So: nothing to add, and ShazamTool's honest `shazam_failed:<code>` stays the truth-teller —
         if catalog matching is still refused on device, THAT is the signal, not a missing key. -->
</dict>
</plist>
